---
description: Guardrails for editing nexlayer.yaml — the Nexlayer deployment file
globs: "**/nexlayer.yaml,**/nexlayer.yml"
alwaysApply: false
---

You are editing a Nexlayer deployment file. It is validated by the platform before deploy, so wrong guesses fail loudly and cost a round trip.

- Validate with `nexlayer_validate_yaml` after every edit, before `nexlayer_deploy`.
- Every pod needs `servicePorts`. At least one pod needs a `path`, or nothing is reachable from the internet.
- Pod names become internal DNS (`{name}.pod`), so keep them valid DNS labels.
- Service-to-service URLs use `{name}.pod:{port}`. Browser-facing variables (`NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, `VITE_*`, `REACT_APP_*`) must use `<% URL %>` — a browser cannot resolve `.pod`.
- Never mount a volume at a database's data directory root; mount a subdirectory instead.
- Images must be built for `linux/amd64` and pushed before they are referenced.

For anything beyond a field edit, load the `nexlayer-deploy` skill.
